Executive Technical Summary

Craneware experienced unauthorized access to a subset of its data environment resulting in exfiltration of information. The company confirmed that attackers viewed and removed a significant volume of file names and also accessed and exfiltrated employee information and a subset of customer and partner records.

Craneware has not publicly established the attacker's initial access path, and there is currently no confirmed CVE, credential-compromise path, malware family, ransomware deployment, or publicly established threat-actor attribution associated with the incident.

The company said the attack was contained and customer services remained available. That is an important distinction: confidentiality was demonstrably affected while availability was not publicly reported as affected.

